From 62520b013cd856655176aa60066e7efb8d89c2c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 02:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: the kernel options of the boot menus as
 settings of the display, where the connector names them

Two parameters of drivers that are built into the kernel change what an
HDMI output offers, and were to be put on the kernel line by hand:
i915.hdmi_hdr_gmp (HDR10 and HLG over the HDMI port of Intel graphics of
display version 9, HD and UHD 6xx) and amdgpu.dvbridge_dce (the Dolby
Vision tunnel on the display cores of AMD Polaris and Vega). They become
two expert settings of System > Display, "HDR over HDMI on this Intel
graphics" (videoscreen.hadeshdrgmp) and "Dolby Vision on this Radeon
(experimental)" (videoscreen.hadesdvdce), off by default.

Each is shown only where the connector of the output that Kodi uses
names its parameter in HADES_BOOT_OPTION, an immutable property that the
kernel attaches to those connectors whatever the parameter is now
(linux-9989), so that it can be turned off again as well. Its value is
the one of the boot menus, which keep it ("internal-disks option NAME"
reads it when the output is read, and the setting is set to it without
acting on it); turning it on or off runs "internal-disks option NAME
on|off" (without a shell, with only the system's PATH, behind the busy
dialog), says what came of it, and asks whether to restart now: the
parameter applies from the next start. Where the menus cannot be told,
the setting is not offered. kodi.log says, when the output is read,
which option is offered, what the menus have and what the running
kernel has (/sys/module), and each change and its outcome.

The help texts say in plain words what each does, that the Intel one has
not been seen on a TV (a washed-out picture means the TV does not take
it) and that with a Dolby Vision TV HDR10 and HLG then go as such and not
as Dolby Vision, and that the Radeon one gave a black picture on an RX
550 with an LG G3, how to get back (stop the video), and where the check
of the Dolby Vision output is. Core strings 41090 to 41097, translated in
Estuary (32970 to 32977: es_es, es_ar, es_mx).

What decides (BootOption.h) has nothing of Kodi in it; a host test of it
(45 checks, ten mutants) fails without the change. Every file changed
and those that include a changed header (80) compiled with their
commands of the build.
